ecil 1.2 features=0x0000000a
; C++ (ECIL 1.2, slice S2): a static local whose initializer has a visible side
; effect (a counter) in the constructor of a class with a virtual base (X : virtual
; V; Y : X and Z : X derive from it).  The constructor has two bodies (C1 and C2),
; each with a STATIC_INIT of the same variable (K5a): the counter must be
; bumped exactly once however the objects are built.  The first object built is
; the base-object constructor (C2); then X as a base subobject (Y, Z) and as a complete object again.
; RUN: %ecil-asm %s -o %t.ecil
; RUN: %edg-cir --emit=obj -o %t.o %t.ecil
; RUN: g++ %t.o -o %t.exe
; RUN: %t.exe
; RUN: %edg-cir --emit=obj -O2 -o %t.o2.o %t.ecil
; RUN: g++ %t.o2.o -o %t.o2.exe
; RUN: %t.o2.exe
